	(text "SIZING (design/README 2.2)\nConduction, 80 A: 2 x 0.6 mOhm hot x 80^2 = 7.7 W total. At 10 to 30 A: 0.1 to 1.1 W for these two banks.\nFET: IPT015N10N5 Rds 1.5 mOhm max at Vgs 10 V, Vgs +/-20 V, so 11 V drive and 16 V zeners are in range (p69 needs >= 15 V).\nShunt voltage rule p69: 13S x 5 V = 65 V DC, 130 V peak. 100 V FETs meet DC. Peak: both TVS parts hold it under 100 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 170.18 195.58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a2c6d594-e132-5857-8dad-9099b69c9bb1")
	)
	(text "SOA must cover 600 A prospective for about 50 us. Reworked after gate 3:\n1. Prospective current: 600 A / 4 = 150 A per FET. On-state part: 0.6 mOhm x 600 A = 0.36 V, 216 W bank, nothing.\n2. Turn-off: TI gives only 2 us typ, 20 us max at 20 nF for the DSG pin, pulsed, stopping at LD (section 16.5). Ours is 48 nF, so a bare 220R is unsupported.\n   Q211: base through 220R and D202, about 45 mA, 10k base-emitter. 15R in the collector sets the peak: 0.62 A from 11 V, under the 800 mA rating. All gate charge 844 nC max in about 2 us. 10 us SOA at 54 V is about 300 A per FET: PASSES at 150 A, with sharing unmodelled: scope at bring-up.\n3. Spike: p72 warns fast turn-off raises the top of stack. 4 x 100 uF hybrid, pack EMF behind 2 uH and 90 mOhm (PLAN pack R): peak about 77 V at -20% C. FET stays under 100 V without avalanche."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 182.88 213.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f4519e96-ae71-5014-b2a4-d888c8317749")
	)
	(text "CP1 is 1 uF on sheet 1: 8 x 211 nC max = 1.69 uC at p65's rule, droop 1.7 V from 11 V.\nPDSG not PCHG: p45 PDSG charges the LOAD before DSG closes; PCHG charges a LOW BATTERY. README 2.1 described the PDSG job.\n100R: peak 54.6^2/100 = 29.8 W. VSYS load 1.46 mF (hold-up via Q1101 body diode, plus VSYS bulk): 2.2 J per power-up, tau 0.146 s. PWR263S chart: 10 J at 100 ms.\nSet OTP: Mfg Status Init[FET_EN] = 1 (default 0 is FET test mode: no PDSG, VSYS stays down, the MCU never boots). PREDISCHARGE on, Predischarge Timeout 100 (1.0 s), Stop Delta 2500 mV.\nStop Delta needs under 25 mA, so the timeout must exist: a hard VSYS short ends in SCD.\nEnabled Protections C[SCDL] = 1, SCDL Latch Limit 2, Counter Dec Delay 60 s: a persistent short costs R209 30 J about every 65 s, not every 6 s.\nFirmware reads FET Status first and holds BUCK12_OFF high only while DSG is off, at every predischarge. It never asserts it with DSG on, so an MCU reset keeps compute up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 182.88 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5d59375a-8fa0-5c1d-8b88-3874a997bc97")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
